    "updated_at": "2020-05-31T19:11:10Z",
    "body": "Well, it seems this isn't exactly a bug, as @matchai has told me...\r\n\r\n> \"prefix\" means two things, sorta\r\n> people use it to mean a prefix to the module, within it, and also the sections between modules that are unstyled\r\n> unfortunately, changing this would be a breaking change for those who intended it to not replace the \"with\" part of the module\r\n\r\n> we are keeping our hands off of anything that changes module affixes until format strings are merged, as that feature will fix all of em\r\n\r\nSo, I guess just wait for a bit, it won't be too long.",
