    "updated_at": "2020-05-31T19:13:29Z",
    "body": "Hey @emarsk! 👋\r\n\r\nUnfortunately, this is working as intended, but still in a confusing manner. We use the term `prefix` to mean the part of a module before the symbol, as well as the module affixes (e.g. \"on\", \"is\", \"with\" between modules). Making any changes to this behavior would be a breaking change to those who expect it to work the way it currently does.\r\n\r\nWe're working to remove the whole notion of \"prefix\" and \"suffix\" as part of #1057, which should let folks customize the prompt as they like. Please keep an eye on that issue for updates. 😄 ",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
